class DisjointSet:
    def __init__(self, n):
        self.parent = list(range(n))
        self.rank = [0] * n                # upper bound on tree height.

    def find(self, x):
        while self.parent[x] != x:
            x = self.parent[x]
        return x

    def union(self, x, y):
        rx, ry = self.find(x), self.find(y)
        if rx == ry:
            return False
        if self.rank[rx] < self.rank[ry]:
            rx, ry = ry, rx                # make rx the higher (or equal) rank.
        self.parent[ry] = rx               # lower rank goes under.
        if self.rank[rx] == self.rank[ry]:
            self.rank[rx] += 1             # equal ranks: height grows by one.
        return True
```

| Ranks of the two roots | New root | New root's rank |
|---|---|---|
| 3 and 1. | the rank-3 root. | stays 3. |
| 2 and 2. | either one. | becomes 3. |
| 0 and 0 (two singletons). | either one. | becomes 1. |

